Two differs live here, sharing picoprefix.h and psram_stub.c.

  diff_main.c  -> picodiff : CONTROL map (byte path vs Pico nibble-packed)
  visdiff_main.c -> visdiff : VISUAL map (the 4bpp/D16 safety net)

Build both the same way; only the final link differs (see each file's header).
visdiff exists BEFORE any visual writer is converted, deliberately: the 16-bit
LCD attempt failed because one writer out of many was converted and the rest
still emitted the old format. Re-run visdiff after each single conversion and a
missed writer shows up as a per-pixel mismatch, offline, instead of as a sheared
picture on the device. Baseline today (nothing converted yet):

  sq3 115 pics / pq2 78 / kq4 150, 0 differ  -- the harness agreeing with itself

NB under HAVE_PICO the decoder DEFERS every index_data allocation to its caller,
so both differs must supply visual/priority/aux buffers themselves.

VGA (2026-09-30, branch pico-sci1): visdiff also handles SCI01 VGA games. A game
with a palette 999 resource is switched to SCI_VERSION_01_VGA (the resource map
alone says SCI0 for Jones in the Fast Lane; SCIVERSION=<n> overrides), the static
palette is passed to both decoders, the EGA dither is skipped, and the priority
map is diffed too. The Pico side now decodes as on the device: the pic is stored
to (stub) PSRAM and read through the stream cache with resource == NULL, so code
that touches the resource pointer directly crashes here, not on the device (each
pic runs in a child process; RAWPTR=1 passes res->data instead). DUMP=<dir>
writes the Pico visual map as picNNN.ppm; a run where every pic is one colour
fails. Baseline: sq3 115 / kq4 150 / pq2 78 / colonel 88 / jones 7, 0 differ.
Build the Pico copy with the shipping defines: -DHAVE_PICO=1 -DPICO_DECODE_CONTROL_MAP=1.

--- picodiff (control map) ---

Decodes a pic's CONTROL map twice -- once through the desktop byte-per-pixel path
and once through the Pico nibble-packed path -- and diffs them. Compiles a SECOND
copy of sci_pic_0.c with -DHAVE_PICO, renaming its exported symbols (picoprefix.h)
so both decoders link together; psram_stub.c backs the PSRAM API with plain RAM.

This is what localised the KQ4 "Rosella swims on the lawn" bug entirely offline.

  cd tests/picodiff
  cp ../../src/gfx/resource/sci_pic_0.c pico_pic.c
  gcc -c -fgnu89-inline -w -DHAVE_CONFIG_H=1 -DX_DISPLAY_MISSING=1 -DHAVE_PICO=1 \
      -DPICO_DECODE_CONTROL_MAP=1 -include picoprefix.h \
      -I. -I../../src/gfx/resource -I../../src/include -I../../build \
      -I/usr/include/SDL2 -D_REENTRANT -o pico_pic.o pico_pic.c
  LIBS=$(find ../../build -name '*.a' | tr '\n' ' ')
  gcc -fgnu89-inline -w -DHAVE_CONFIG_H=1 -DX_DISPLAY_MISSING=1 \
      -I../../src/include -I../../build -I/usr/include/SDL2 -D_REENTRANT \
      -o picodiff diff_main.c pico_pic.o psram_stub.c \
      -Wl,--start-group $LIBS -Wl,--end-group -lSDL2 -lm -lz -lpthread -ldl
  ./picodiff /path/to/game 25 1 3        # pic numbers
  DUMPMAP=1 ./picodiff /path/to/game 25  # ASCII maps when they differ
